															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/smaugnolia" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1423461); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1423461&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606921229" alt="Smaugnolia" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1423461)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/smaugnolia" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1423461); return false;" >Smaugnolia</a></span> <span class="odate time_1472716682 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Sep 2016 07:58</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2582210">
									

<p>I genuinely adore this one, in concept, and almost entirely in execution. An eldritch entity that has a crush on the foundation is brilliant, but I can't overlook the fact that this object is not Thaumiel. It's useful, but plenty of SCPs are useful, useful does not make something Thaumiel. To be Thaumiel an object has to be a reliable foundation asset. It should be reliable, well understood, trusted, and capable of being relied on in an emergency scenario. This is none of those things. This is an unknown, uncontained entity of apparently vast intellect and power (knowledge of advanced technology and ability to deliver communications, apparently through teleportation), and we only have its word to go on as to its intentions. On top of that, It apparently has a great ability to spy on and gather information about the foundation, that fact alone could qualify it for Keter status.</p>
<p>Keeping it happy and utilizing its information can be part of the containment procedures, as that seems to be what is currently effective, and it's useful, but it's firmly in Euclid/Keter territory. There's nothing Thaumiel about this, and I can't in good conscience upvote it with such a glaring error.</p>
<p>Edit: Following the reclassification and containment procedures changes, this is an absolutely firm upvote from me.</p>

							</div>

								
