			<div class="content" id="post-content-2583721">
									

<p>This was written on a whim with the basic intention of seeing whether I could go directly from idea to positively-rated mainsite article with an idea as inherently goofy as this one. This isn't an excuse for a poor-quality piece and I know that, but it's been positively received.</p>
<p>However, most of the upvotes seem to be coming from new or otherwise non-contributor members, which means that the core of the community, my fellow writers (such as yourself), don't care for the piece. Yours is the first piece of extensive feedback that I've gotten from a successful author for the site, and honestly, between this and the increasing number of author downvotes, I'm beginning to feel inclined to move the piece to the sandbox and clear the slate here on the main site.</p>
<p>I know that you and I don't usually get along, and I know that you clearly didn't enjoy reading the piece, so I appreciate you taking the time to write this review and will likely make edits based on it sometime in the near future. Thank you for your feedback.</p>

